  "term": "orthogenesis",
  "definition": "Orthogenesis is the historical idea that evolution proceeds along fixed, predetermined lines because of an internal life principle, rather than being chiefly shaped by environmental selection. In this view, natural selection is only secondary to a built-in direction of organic change.",
